# Fuzz seeds are byte fixtures, not text. An http seed ends in the chunked
# terminator's CRLF CRLF, an ACL blob is little-endian binary, a resume cookie
# carries a native-endian magic — none of it survives EOL normalization, and a
# checkout under core.autocrlf would silently corrupt the corpus. Marking the
# tree binary also stops the whitespace checks from reporting protocol bytes as
# stray blank lines at EOF.
fuzz/corpus/** binary
